 -->\r\n\r\nThis adds an implementation-settable version property that can be used to display the application version. This version is set at the time that the `assemble` command is run by passing in the `--openmrs-version` property. While SemVer are encouraged, you can actually use any string that makes sense.\r\n\r\nBy default, this version is displayed on the login screen and primary navigation. When not set, the version will read \"Prerelease\" (this is translatable). For no version display, set `--openmrs-version ''`.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n<!-- Required if you are making UI changes. -->\r\n\r\n<img width=\"452\" height=\"462\" alt=\"Screenshot of login screen displaying version\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e595d38f-8f7e-4c73-bd23-b0e7a75943a5\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"234\" height=\"51\" alt=\"Screenshot of primary navigation displaying version\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/af1ab9d6-4d4f-42bb-918e-dbf029720fe0\" />\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\n<!-- Paste the link to the Jira ticket here if one exists. -->\r\n<!-- https://issues.openmrs.org/browse/O3- -->\r\n\r\n## Other\r\n<!-- Anything not covered above -->\r\n\r\nI've rejected at least one attempt at doing something similar using the configuration system. Configuration files just aren't the right place for this. Realistically, we should probably have a global property to control this, but that requires some coordination with the backend team.\r\n\r\nThe version number is generally available as the `window.openmrsVersion` property. This may be slightly confusing with the `spaVersion` property. The `spaVersion` property is the version of the app shell / root container and is mostly intended for technical audiences / debugging. `openmrsVersion` is intended for user display.\r\n","freshness":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","lastSyncedAt":"2026-10-31T16:11:06.195Z","stale":false}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015G7uc